      "math_academy_id": "e-12869",
      "problem": "Find the $y$-intercept of the line that passes through the point $(-1, 4)$ and has a slope of $2.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since the line passes through the point $(-1,4)$ and its slope is $2$, we substitute $x=-1$, $y=4,$ and $m=2$ into the equation in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\ty &= mx + b \\\n\t(4) &= (2)(-1) + b \\\n\t4 &= -2 + b \\\n\t6 &= b\n}\n$$\n\nSo, the $y$-intercept is $b=6.$ The coordinates of the $y$-intercept are $(0,6).$",
